      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the remainders when the sum of the three integers is divided by 24. Let's denote the three integers as \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). According to the problem, we have the following congruences:\n\n\\[a \\equiv 10 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\\[b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\\[c \\equiv 12 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\nWe need to find the remainder when \\(a + b + c\\) is divided by 24. First, we add the congruences together:\n\n\\[a + b + c \\equiv 10 + 4 + 12 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the sum on the right side:\n\n\\[10 + 4 + 12 = 26\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[a + b + c \\equiv 26 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when 26 is divided by 24. We can do this by subtracting 24 from 26:\n\n\\[26 - 24 = 2\\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\(a + b + c\\) is divided by 24 is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{2}\\]",
